WEBVTT

00:01.140 --> 00:04.390
You still haven't been able 
to track down Rikka-san?

00:04.390 --> 00:07.140
I do get some eyewitness 
accounts every now and then,

00:07.140 --> 00:09.860
but nothing solid.

00:09.860 --> 00:12.240
It's already the middle of July.

00:12.240 --> 00:15.870
It's been nearly a year since she disappeared.

00:15.870 --> 00:18.440
I've told all the yokai 
and ayakashi in the land

00:18.440 --> 00:21.870
to contact me immediately if they see her,

00:21.870 --> 00:25.830
but there's no guarantee I'll 
hear something immediately.

00:25.830 --> 00:31.450
I'm sure she's also traveling around to 
places where there are only a few ayakashi.

00:31.450 --> 00:36.620
It'd be quite helpful if she could 
just stay in one spot for a while.

00:37.260 --> 00:41.770
You and Rikka-san did actually get 
along at one point, didn't you?

00:41.770 --> 00:44.020
Well, somewhat.

00:44.020 --> 00:48.710
When she was at my mansion, 
we even had a conversation like this...

00:49.200 --> 00:50.440
Kotoko-san...

00:50.440 --> 00:53.740
What are you scared of?

00:54.350 --> 00:55.990
Well...

00:55.990 --> 00:58.950
I'd say a hot cup of tea is scary.

00:59.680 --> 01:02.530
That's exactly what I hate about you.

01:02.530 --> 01:03.450
Huh?

01:03.450 --> 01:06.460
How could there possibly be 
a problem with my answer?

01:06.460 --> 01:08.490
I asked you a proper question,

01:08.490 --> 01:13.500
but you blew it off like you 
were reading "Manju Kowai."

01:13.500 --> 01:17.390
Also, don't just suddenly use 
the final punchline like that.

01:14.840 --> 01:17.180
<b>Rook</b>

01:14.840 --> 01:18.430
<b>Gold
General</b>

01:17.390 --> 01:19.650
You're spoiling the story.

01:19.650 --> 01:22.830
How do you even spoil a classic rakugo story?

01:22.830 --> 01:27.630
I mean, I'm not sure how to 
answer your question, though.

01:27.630 --> 01:30.450
You're a girl, so are you scared of spiders?

01:30.450 --> 01:33.320
I just listened to the problems 
of a giant spider the other day.

01:33.320 --> 01:35.730
I can't say I was that scared.

01:35.730 --> 01:40.370
It may have had long legs, but I could've 
easily crushed its head with my fist.

01:40.370 --> 01:41.740
What about snakes, then?

01:41.740 --> 01:43.240
I'm used to them.

01:43.240 --> 01:44.840
What about bugs?

01:45.320 --> 01:47.620
Though I'm sure you're probably 
fine with those, as well.

01:47.620 --> 01:49.070
If I was scared of bugs,

01:49.070 --> 01:52.960
I wouldn't be able to go to the mountains 
or deserted houses where yokai live.

01:52.960 --> 01:55.780
Okay, then what if Kuro ends up hating you?

01:55.780 --> 01:59.510
Oh, I guess he already does.

01:59.300 --> 02:01.470
<b>Bishop</b>

01:59.510 --> 02:01.470
He does <i>not</i> hate me.

02:01.470 --> 02:05.580
Still, every relationship has ups and downs 
when you've been in it long enough.

02:05.580 --> 02:07.310
That's nothing to be scared of.

02:07.310 --> 02:11.440
Then I guess you're probably not 
afraid of Kuro tossing you aside.

02:11.440 --> 02:14.840
Oh, wait... I guess he's already 
basically tossed you aside.

02:15.570 --> 02:17.570
"Basically," my foot.

02:17.570 --> 02:21.530
For one thing, if that ever were the scenario, 
I could fix it using any means necessary.

02:21.530 --> 02:25.240
You do realize that makes you 
sound like a stalker, right?

02:25.240 --> 02:30.060
You have some nerve, insulting me like that 
when I'm letting you stay in my home.

02:30.060 --> 02:33.380
Well, your parents like me.

02:33.380 --> 02:35.390
That's just the thing, though.

02:35.390 --> 02:39.120
What could my parents possibly like about 
a woman who resembles a sukima onna?

02:39.120 --> 02:41.800
How can you say such cruel 
things about the cousin

02:41.800 --> 02:43.510
your boyfriend cares so deeply for?

02:43.850 --> 02:49.640
And that's exactly why no good would come 
of me telling you what I'm scared of.

02:50.090 --> 02:51.650
Well, then, Rikka-san...

02:51.650 --> 02:54.020
What are you afraid of?

02:55.890 --> 02:58.320
You scare me more than anything,

02:58.780 --> 03:00.530
Kotoko-san.

03:00.530 --> 03:04.060
Yeah, Rikka-san totally hates you.

03:04.060 --> 03:06.570
What?! Wait, doesn't the last thing she said

03:06.570 --> 03:10.540
make it sound like she finds me endearing?

03:10.540 --> 03:13.040
I mean, see? "Manju Kowai."

03:15.350 --> 03:19.300
I wonder what she's up to right now.

03:19.940 --> 03:22.800
<b>Two Months Earlier</b>

03:34.690 --> 03:36.690
Hello, Sakuragawa-san.

03:36.690 --> 03:41.800
Oh. Hello, Manager. Is something wrong?

03:41.800 --> 03:45.410
I forgot to take the tape 
off of room 305's mailbox.

03:45.410 --> 03:50.690
Sorry I didn't realize it, even though 
you moved here a week ago.

03:50.690 --> 03:53.930
No, it's fine. It's not like I'd get any letters.

03:53.930 --> 03:55.330
Kazuyuki!

03:55.330 --> 03:58.050
Oh, isn't this the new tenant?

03:58.050 --> 04:00.890
Yeah, she moved in last week.

04:00.890 --> 04:02.650
I'm Sakuragawa Rikka.

04:02.650 --> 04:05.470
This is my girlfriend, Oki Marumi.

04:05.470 --> 04:07.170
It's a pleasure to meet you!

04:07.170 --> 04:08.850
Are you headed out somewhere?

04:08.850 --> 04:11.060
Yes. I'm heading to the horse races.

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
56,231st

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
Kantou

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
<b>Race</b>

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
SUIHANABI PRIZE

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
<b>Quinella</b>

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
Horses, eh?

04:12.690 --> 04:16.350
How unexpected. I hope you win.

04:16.350 --> 04:19.340
Thanks. Now, if you'll excuse me.

04:20.700 --> 04:22.700
She's so pretty!

04:23.670 --> 04:26.260
But you're the only girl for me, Marumi.

04:26.260 --> 04:30.120
I know. She doesn't seem like your type.

04:30.120 --> 04:34.820
But you know... She has this 
extraordinary aura around her.

04:35.580 --> 04:37.500
Say, Kazuyuki...

04:37.500 --> 04:40.880
Isn't her apartment...

04:57.680 --> 04:58.940
Sakuragawa-san?!

04:59.300 --> 05:02.850
Sh-She tried to save my child, and then she...

05:02.850 --> 05:04.610
Marumi! Call an ambulance!

05:04.610 --> 05:05.700
R-Right!

05:05.700 --> 05:07.510
Sakuragawa-san!

05:07.510 --> 05:09.130
Don't worry.

05:09.130 --> 05:10.620
I'm fine.

05:14.830 --> 05:16.380
Er, but...

05:16.380 --> 05:19.810
Wait, the blood... 
Um, you don't have any wounds?

05:19.810 --> 05:20.730
Not really.

05:20.730 --> 05:22.090
N-Not really?!

05:22.090 --> 05:26.450
But that's impossible. You flew so far...

05:26.450 --> 05:30.350
It's in period dramas all the time. 
The character is cut many times, but isn't hurt.

05:30.350 --> 05:33.600
Yes, like being struck by 
the blunt side of a sword.

05:33.600 --> 05:36.600
The blunt side of... a vehicle?

05:37.350 --> 05:41.550
I've been tasked by my uncle 
to manage these apartments,

05:41.550 --> 05:46.490
and there's an apartment where three suicide 
victims appeared within the last year.

05:46.800 --> 05:49.870
It's what you'd call a stigmatized property.

05:49.870 --> 05:53.850
305 finally had a new tenant...

05:53.850 --> 05:55.620
and that was Sakuragawa-san.

05:55.900 --> 06:01.060
If it ends up becoming four... it's 
seriously one hell of a stigmatized property.

06:01.060 --> 06:06.220
Maybe we should let one of Sakuragawa-san's 
relatives know about the accident.

06:06.220 --> 06:10.290
But she moved in with just 
one piece of luggage.

06:10.290 --> 06:10.840
What?

06:10.840 --> 06:16.260
Like she fled with the minimal amount of 
clothes and whatever else she could grab.

06:16.260 --> 06:20.770
I called my uncle, and he said 
she didn't have a cosigner,

06:20.770 --> 06:24.670
plus he couldn't get a hold 
of any family or relatives.

06:24.670 --> 06:27.780
She looked like she had a history. 
I guess she really does.

06:27.780 --> 06:32.030
And that's why she had no problem 
renting a room with a history.

06:32.160 --> 06:34.540
SUIHANABI PRIZE

06:32.160 --> 06:36.460
<i>With less than 200 to go, Number 10, 
Sunagimo Shioaji, has the lead.</i>

06:34.540 --> 06:37.550
Oh, isn't that Sakuragawa-san's?

06:37.550 --> 06:40.420
Yeah, it was on the ground earlier.

06:40.440 --> 06:42.530
<i>Yagen Nankotsu has caught 
up and taken the lead!</i>

06:42.530 --> 06:47.560
<i>But Number 10, Sunagimo Shioaji, surpasses 
Yagen Nankotsu and wins the race!</i>

06:44.170 --> 06:46.600
Hey, she won!

06:46.600 --> 06:47.560
No way!

06:47.560 --> 06:50.300
I wonder if she actually 
knows a lot about horse races.

06:50.300 --> 06:51.850
How much did she win?

06:51.850 --> 06:57.830
Um... She chose a quinella, 
which pays back 13,000 yen,

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Win</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Place</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Bracket Quinella</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Quinella</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Exact</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Trio</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Trifecta</b>

06:53.300 --> 06:57.640
<b>Wide</b>

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
56,231st

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
Kantou

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
<b>Race</b>

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
SUIHANABI PRIZE

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
<b>Quinella</b>

06:57.830 --> 06:59.560
Total

06:57.830 --> 07:01.310
which is multiplied by 20,000, so she got...

06:59.560 --> 07:01.310
<b>Total</b>

07:01.310 --> 07:03.310
2.6 million yen?!

07:03.310 --> 07:04.090
Huh?!

07:04.090 --> 07:06.530
Er, maybe I just calculated wrong.

07:07.480 --> 07:10.780
Sunagimo Shioaji... So her ticket pays 
out least a hundred times more?

07:10.780 --> 07:12.550
That's amazing...

07:15.180 --> 07:16.820
Sakuragawa-san.

07:16.820 --> 07:19.080
Sorry for all the trouble this afternoon.

07:19.080 --> 07:20.520
Weren't you in the hospital?

07:20.520 --> 07:21.960
I was released.

07:21.960 --> 07:24.960
As you can see, I'm perfectly fine.

07:24.960 --> 07:29.440
I-I see... Well, I'm definitely 
happy to hear that.

07:29.720 --> 07:32.800
It's a miracle you survived 
an accident like that.

07:33.070 --> 07:34.800
Here's a token of my gratitude.

07:33.070 --> 07:34.800
We stretched the limits of low carbs.

07:34.800 --> 07:36.200
Oh, we couldn't...

07:36.200 --> 07:38.930
Sakuragawa-san! This is a ticket that 
pays out at least a hundred times!

07:38.930 --> 07:43.440
Oh, you picked it up. 
Thank you very much.

07:43.440 --> 07:46.830
B-But the payout is really huge...

07:43.440 --> 07:52.990
Konno

07:46.830 --> 07:51.200
Oh, it's really not that rare. Goodbye.

07:51.200 --> 07:52.990
Um, Sakuragawa-san.

07:53.980 --> 07:57.570
Why don't we drink together?

08:00.030 --> 08:04.020
I had heard that three people 
committed suicide here,

08:04.020 --> 08:05.380
but I wasn't bothered by it.

08:05.380 --> 08:08.950
And it made it easier for 
me to rent the place.

08:09.760 --> 08:12.260
Has anything unusual happened to you?

08:12.620 --> 08:15.500
Like any strange sounds at night?

08:15.500 --> 08:17.980
Or seeing things out of 
the corners of your eyes?

08:17.980 --> 08:19.520
No, nothing.

08:19.520 --> 08:23.640
But you're not worried 
about ghosts and stuff?

08:23.640 --> 08:26.630
The first guy who committed 
suicide in that apartment

08:26.630 --> 08:29.570
mentioned something about 
a face in the ceiling...

08:29.570 --> 08:32.780
It would be quite nice if 
something like that could kill me.

08:33.160 --> 08:38.030
Besides, most stigmatized properties 
have quite logical explanations.

08:38.030 --> 08:41.660
So why did the first man commit suicide?

08:43.750 --> 08:47.170
The first guy was single and in his forties,

08:47.170 --> 08:52.190
and apparently, he suffered a huge nervous 
breakdown due to trouble at work.

08:52.190 --> 08:56.300
Meaning he had a reason to commit suicide 
that had nothing to do with the room.

08:56.650 --> 09:00.560
And because of that suicide, you had 
no choice but to lower the rent,

09:00.560 --> 09:03.310
making it more accessible 
to people with dark histories.

09:03.310 --> 09:08.390
Which probably means the second person 
also had some reason for their suicide.

09:08.390 --> 09:09.940
Yes, well...

09:09.940 --> 09:13.120
The second was a woman in her late twenties

09:13.120 --> 09:16.320
who was apparently dumped 
in a horrible way by her boyfriend,

09:16.320 --> 09:19.700
so she came to live here since she 
had nowhere to live or work anymore.

09:19.700 --> 09:25.960
She made a fresh start, but then 
committed suicide three months later.

09:25.960 --> 09:27.210
She left no note or will.

09:27.210 --> 09:30.760
It was as though they were influenced by 
the will of the last guy who committed suicide.

09:30.760 --> 09:32.970
Well, she was someone who very well

09:32.970 --> 09:35.970
could have committed suicide 
right after her breakup, right?

09:35.970 --> 09:38.920
She managed to initially push through that,

09:38.920 --> 09:42.020
but in the end, she couldn't get 
over the pain of the breakup,

09:42.020 --> 09:44.670
and then, one day, took her own life.

09:44.670 --> 09:47.390
It's quite an everyday occurrence.

09:45.730 --> 09:47.850
Mugijitsu

09:45.730 --> 09:47.850
The power of barley

09:47.390 --> 09:50.360
The same can't be said 
for the third victim, though.

09:50.770 --> 09:53.080
He was a man who was nearing thirty,

09:53.080 --> 09:56.740
but he also committed suicide within 
the first three months of moving in.

09:56.740 --> 09:59.690
His work was going well, and 
he was even in a relationship.

09:59.690 --> 10:03.200
There was no apparent reason for suicide, 
and we couldn't find a note or a will.

10:03.200 --> 10:06.910
But when the police decided 
to investigate the death,

10:06.910 --> 10:10.000
we found out that this 
man was the ex-boyfriend

10:10.000 --> 10:12.210
of the woman who had 
committed suicide there prior.

10:12.210 --> 10:14.820
The one who supposedly 
dumped her in an awful way?

10:14.820 --> 10:16.800
Yes. That's weird, right?

10:16.800 --> 10:18.860
There's no way he just happened to move into

10:18.860 --> 10:21.140
the apartment where his 
ex-girlfriend committed suicide.

10:21.140 --> 10:25.270
On the other hand, it's hard to imagine he 
intentionally moved in knowing that, too.

10:25.270 --> 10:30.650
<b>No Trespassing</b>

10:25.270 --> 10:30.650
MPD

10:25.650 --> 10:29.040
That's why the police thought 
there might be something behind this

10:29.040 --> 10:30.650
and investigated further,

10:30.650 --> 10:33.260
but there were no indications 
that this was a murder,

10:33.260 --> 10:35.970
so they determined that his 
suicide was done impulsively.

10:35.970 --> 10:40.700
After the first two suicides, 
bad rumors started to circulate,

10:40.700 --> 10:43.490
but that was all affirmed 
with the third death.

10:43.910 --> 10:46.930
It's great if this doesn't 
faze you, Sakuragawa-san,

10:46.930 --> 10:50.790
but if it bothers you even 
a little, please let us know.

10:50.790 --> 10:52.810
Thank you very much for your concern.

10:52.810 --> 10:54.040
Um...

10:54.040 --> 10:57.420
So why did you end up in that 
apartment, Sakuragawa-san?

10:58.520 --> 11:01.760
I heard that you barely made 
any moving preparations,

11:01.760 --> 11:05.990
but you don't seem to be 
suffering financially, either.

11:08.480 --> 11:12.600
My cousin, who's three years younger 
than me, ended up with an awful girl.

11:12.600 --> 11:13.790
Cousin?

11:13.790 --> 11:15.520
I figured that even if I did nothing,

11:15.520 --> 11:18.590
their relationship wouldn't have lasted.

11:18.590 --> 11:21.150
But instead, they just seem 
to be getting closer.

11:22.960 --> 11:27.040
I realized that this couldn't continue, 
so I tried to put an end to it,

11:27.040 --> 11:30.460
but she truly is... such an awful girl,

11:31.630 --> 11:33.610
and she just refuses to leave him alone.

11:33.610 --> 11:34.540
I see...

11:34.540 --> 11:37.760
If my cousin and I became 
proper human beings,

11:37.760 --> 11:39.980
we would definitely be 
able to get rid of her,

11:39.980 --> 11:44.050
so I tried various methods, 
but the girl kept interfering,

11:44.050 --> 11:48.180
and in the end, I ended up being 
the one who had to go into hiding.

11:48.180 --> 11:50.540
Proper... human beings?

11:50.540 --> 11:52.300
There's no deep meaning behind it.

11:52.300 --> 11:54.270
She's just the farthest thing from proper.

11:54.270 --> 11:58.960
So... I decided to rent 
that apartment temporarily.

11:58.960 --> 12:03.070
It'll be nothing but trouble if that girl finds us, 
so I probably won't be able to stay there long.

12:05.220 --> 12:08.800
Don't worry. I haven't done anything illegal.

12:08.800 --> 12:11.580
But if my cousin continues down this path,

12:11.580 --> 12:16.130
he's just going to be dumped by that girl 
in an awful way, and end up unhappy.

12:16.130 --> 12:20.340
He probably doesn't realize that, though, 
because he's always been a bit dense.

12:21.590 --> 12:24.090
I want to take care of this 
as soon as possible.

12:24.090 --> 12:27.480
This cousin must be very important to you.

12:29.820 --> 12:32.540
He was supposed to be mine.

12:38.360 --> 12:43.030
<b>Rikka Returns</b>

12:45.530 --> 12:49.280
Konno

12:47.150 --> 12:49.280
Huh? What brings you here?

12:49.280 --> 12:50.900
Especially at this hour.

12:50.900 --> 12:52.500
I'm sorry to come by so late at night,

12:52.500 --> 12:56.730
but it seems my cousin and that girl 
have figured out where I was.

12:56.730 --> 12:59.610
I know this is sudden, but I'm 
going to disappear for a while.

12:59.610 --> 13:00.380
Huh?

13:00.740 --> 13:03.380
It's not much, but please take this 
for all the inconvenience I've caused.

13:03.380 --> 13:04.380
Huh? Um...

13:04.380 --> 13:10.390
There may be even more bad rumors 
about that apartment as soon as I leave.

13:10.390 --> 13:12.860
Uh, but...

13:14.300 --> 13:17.650
My cousin and that girl will come here soon.

13:18.030 --> 13:20.840
I'm sure that girl will give you

13:20.840 --> 13:24.400
a perfectly logical explanation 
for why all the suicides happened.

13:24.400 --> 13:28.030
You'll have no trouble renting out 
that apartment after that.

13:28.780 --> 13:31.280
Thanks for everything.

13:31.280 --> 13:32.290
Please take care.

13:36.990 --> 13:37.790
Um...

13:38.290 --> 13:40.920
I hope everything works out 
with you and your cousin.

13:47.060 --> 13:48.300
Is she just that intuitive,

13:48.300 --> 13:51.130
or did she just happen 
to pick the right future?

13:51.760 --> 13:54.240
Either way, it appears 
she got away just in time.

13:55.100 --> 13:58.100
Konno

13:55.550 --> 13:58.100
Sorry to visit you so early 
on a weekend morning.

13:58.100 --> 14:00.380
My name is Iwanaga Kotoko.

14:00.380 --> 14:03.110
This is Sakuragawa Rikka-san's cousin,

14:03.110 --> 14:06.980
Sakuragawa Kuro-san. He's also my boyfriend.

14:06.980 --> 14:09.240
Thank you for taking care of Rikka-san.

14:09.240 --> 14:12.870
<i>Wait, this is the awful girl?</i>

14:12.870 --> 14:14.950
Is there something about me 
that concerns you?

14:14.950 --> 14:18.140
Oh, no. It's not a huge deal...

14:18.140 --> 14:21.840
You just seem very different from 
how Sakuragawa-san described you.

14:21.840 --> 14:26.290
I hadn't imagined that Rikka-san's cousin's 
girlfriend looked so much like a doll.

14:26.290 --> 14:29.730
A doll? But there's definitely 
blood flowing through my veins.

14:29.730 --> 14:34.620
And Iwanaga is actually quite hairy, 
so she's very different from a doll.

14:34.620 --> 14:36.340
Who are you calling hairy?!

14:36.340 --> 14:38.310
I'm not hairy at all!

14:38.310 --> 14:39.950
You were even lamenting the fact

14:39.950 --> 14:44.030
that you couldn't enjoy drinking 
wakamezake from my crotch!

14:44.030 --> 14:46.160
I definitely don't remember lamenting that,

14:46.160 --> 14:49.190
nor do I even know what 
kind of sake that is.

14:49.190 --> 14:52.690
I'm sure it's something that'll 
further lower my reputation.

14:52.690 --> 14:53.910
You don't know what it is?

14:53.910 --> 14:56.370
Then let's try some tonight!

14:56.370 --> 14:57.910
<i>Yeah, I guess you can say</i>

14:57.910 --> 14:59.920
<i>that this girl is pretty awful.</i>

15:00.290 --> 15:01.290
Um...

15:01.290 --> 15:04.480
Why are you looking for that girl?

15:04.480 --> 15:06.550
She didn't seem like a bad person.

15:06.550 --> 15:12.310
Actually, aren't you the two 
who made her go into hiding?

15:12.310 --> 15:16.510
It's not like we want to harm Rikka-san, either.

15:16.510 --> 15:19.840
You could say it'd be a huge issue for society

15:19.840 --> 15:22.350
if we let her run free for too long.

15:22.900 --> 15:28.760
In actuality, we might be the ones 
being trapped by Rikka-san.

15:28.760 --> 15:32.520
Did Rikka-san say anything 
about what she was planning to do?

15:32.520 --> 15:34.240
Um...

15:34.240 --> 15:37.140
<i>I probably shouldn't tell them 
what we were talking about.</i>

15:37.140 --> 15:39.340
<i>Especially the part about 
her wanting to break them up.</i>

15:39.340 --> 15:42.970
She did talk about wanting to figure 
out what she was going to do now,

15:42.970 --> 15:45.070
but didn't mention any details.

15:45.070 --> 15:50.170
We managed to track her down today 
because she stayed in one spot for so long,

15:50.170 --> 15:52.550
but I'm sure she won't 
make the same mistake again.

15:52.550 --> 15:54.510
It's such a pain.

15:56.390 --> 15:58.310
Thank you for everything today.

15:58.310 --> 16:01.180
If you happen to remember 
anything about Rikka-san,

16:01.180 --> 16:03.210
please contact me.

16:03.210 --> 16:04.300
Right...

16:04.300 --> 16:06.820
Also if you're ever in any trouble.

16:07.670 --> 16:12.350
Oh, I guess you might actually be troubled 
about this stigmatized apartment.

16:12.350 --> 16:13.280
Yes...

16:13.280 --> 16:15.090
Have no fear.

16:15.090 --> 16:18.800
There aren't any ghosts, curses, or other 
strange things attached to this place.

16:18.800 --> 16:21.160
If you don't let any more 
suicidal people rent it,

16:21.160 --> 16:23.280
the same thing won't happen again.

16:23.280 --> 16:24.880
Huh? But...

16:24.880 --> 16:26.290
The first suicide victim

16:26.290 --> 16:29.360
clearly had a reason to go through with it.

16:29.930 --> 16:32.920
The second was in a very 
emotionally fragile state,

16:32.920 --> 16:35.550
so it wasn't surprising that 
the same fate awaited her.

16:35.550 --> 16:39.430
The reason the suicides continued 
was partially due to the cheap rent,

16:39.430 --> 16:42.370
but it was really no more than 
an unfortunate coincidence.

16:42.370 --> 16:45.440
But that explanation doesn't 
work for the third guy.

16:45.440 --> 16:48.730
Why would the ex-boyfriend of the girl 
who committed suicide here

16:48.730 --> 16:51.130
bother renting this place,

16:51.130 --> 16:53.820
and then end up committing 
suicide three months later?

16:53.820 --> 16:57.820
Because he just had to find out for himself.

16:58.350 --> 16:59.580
Find out for himself?

16:59.930 --> 17:03.070
If the ex-girlfriend he horribly 
dumped happened to commit suicide,

17:03.070 --> 17:06.170
he may not be judged in the court of law,

17:06.170 --> 17:08.620
but I'm sure those around him blamed him

17:08.620 --> 17:10.300
and gave the cold shoulder.

17:10.710 --> 17:13.220
Even if they broke up 
in a very amicable way,

17:13.220 --> 17:18.900
the girl may have imagined it being 
much more horrible than it was.

17:18.900 --> 17:25.250
But it's also true that he was a huge 
reason why she ended up dead.

17:25.250 --> 17:29.440
That would probably be 
a big deal for normal people.

17:29.440 --> 17:30.390
I guess you're right.

17:30.390 --> 17:34.490
Unless they were completely insensitive, 
they probably felt a little guilty.

17:34.490 --> 17:39.370
But why this apartment? 
It's like their guilt would've multiplied.

17:39.370 --> 17:43.680
And that's exactly why he 
wanted to find out for sure

17:43.680 --> 17:48.420
that the reason she committed suicide was 
because of the apartment and not him.

17:48.740 --> 17:53.420
Because he felt so guilty, he wanted to 
find something he could shift the blame to.

17:54.290 --> 17:57.990
Once he died, rumors about this 
apartment being haunted spread

17:57.990 --> 18:01.830
because consecutive tenants 
died by suicide, right?

18:01.830 --> 18:02.560
Yes.

18:02.560 --> 18:07.310
Some supernatural power was at work in
the room, driving its tenants to their deaths.

18:07.310 --> 18:10.810
The series of suicides in that 
room started long ago.

18:10.810 --> 18:14.730
The hair of those who died is buried in the walls and ceiling, et cetera.

18:14.730 --> 18:18.320
Those rumors all sound plausible, 
and will get spread.

18:18.320 --> 18:21.940
Yeah, I actually heard 
something pretty similar.

18:21.940 --> 18:26.540
After the man heard that, he ended up 
blaming this apartment for his ex's death.

18:26.540 --> 18:30.210
And because of that, he might be able 
to escape from feeling responsible.

18:30.210 --> 18:33.970
To confirm if there were any 
actual ghosts in this apartment,

18:33.970 --> 18:35.710
he decided to move in.

18:35.710 --> 18:39.330
It's uncertain if those around 
him would actually believe him.

18:39.330 --> 18:41.900
But if he experienced this for himself,

18:41.900 --> 18:45.550
he could convince himself 
that the suicide wasn't his fault.

18:45.550 --> 18:48.730
That would've been a huge 
weight off his shoulders.

18:48.730 --> 18:51.590
And if he did confirm anything 
ghostly in the apartment,

18:51.590 --> 18:53.480
he was going to leave immediately.

18:53.480 --> 18:58.240
Confirm? But isn't it scarier 
knowing something like that exists?

18:58.240 --> 19:00.600
If there was something 
ghostly haunting this room,

19:00.600 --> 19:03.570
it probably wouldn't have been 
able to do anything once he left.

19:03.570 --> 19:06.250
But his guilt was always with him,

19:06.250 --> 19:09.370
and he couldn't escape from it.

19:09.740 --> 19:12.070
Everyone has different fears.

19:12.070 --> 19:13.720
If anything, at the time,

19:13.720 --> 19:18.280
the man was more scared of his own 
guilt than anything supernatural.

19:19.420 --> 19:22.670
Then why did he also commit suicide?

19:22.670 --> 19:26.070
If he planned to leave if the 
apartment was actually haunted,

19:26.070 --> 19:28.040
there was no reason to feel
pressured to end his life.

19:28.040 --> 19:28.930
You have that backwards.

19:28.930 --> 19:31.020
Three months had passed,

19:31.020 --> 19:36.070
and there was nothing haunting the 
apartment, so he felt pressured to die.

19:36.070 --> 19:39.680
Not only was there nothing in the room,

19:39.680 --> 19:41.150
but he was the cause of her death.

19:41.150 --> 19:43.450
That fact became even clearer.

19:41.150 --> 19:43.450
Day 89  |   Day 90   |   Day 91   |  Day 92
No issues | No issues | No issues | No issues

19:43.450 --> 19:46.200
Which just made his sense of guilt grow,

19:46.640 --> 19:50.210
until his heart could no longer escape it.

19:50.210 --> 19:53.530
So he didn't commit suicide because 
there was something wrong with the room,

19:53.530 --> 19:55.960
but he committed suicide because 
there wasn't anything wrong?

19:55.960 --> 20:01.220
The reason he didn't leave a note was either 
because he wasn't mentally able to...

20:01.220 --> 20:04.160
or because, by dying without leaving a note,

20:04.160 --> 20:07.770
he was trying to make it seem like 
he was also forced into suicide

20:07.770 --> 20:09.970
by something haunting the room.

20:09.970 --> 20:14.030
He wanted to at least make sure he 
wasn't going to be blamed after his death.

20:14.030 --> 20:15.610
It was his final act of resistance.

20:15.610 --> 20:17.740
What a horrible sore loser.

20:17.740 --> 20:24.240
But his narrow-minded family might become 
more generous because of the suicide.

20:24.240 --> 20:26.800
Having a relative who not only 
forced a girl to suicide,

20:26.800 --> 20:28.620
but committed suicide himself,

20:28.910 --> 20:33.120
would be rather rough for those left behind.

20:33.530 --> 20:35.760
The fact that he gave them an escape route

20:35.760 --> 20:37.880
could be considered a final act of kindness

20:38.370 --> 20:41.570
because the man had nowhere 
else to go and had to die.

20:42.910 --> 20:45.630
Well, this is a perfect example

20:45.630 --> 20:48.100
of why you should never get 
involved with the supernatural.

20:48.760 --> 20:52.280
Those two actually seemed 
to get along really well.

20:52.280 --> 20:54.350
Yeah, it seemed like her cousin, especially,

20:54.350 --> 20:57.660
really thought Iwanaga-san was important.

20:57.660 --> 20:59.770
But Iwanaga-san...

21:01.280 --> 21:02.830
was pretty awful.

21:02.830 --> 21:03.780
Yeah.

21:03.780 --> 21:07.090
I wonder if Sakuragawa-san 
was just jealous because

21:07.090 --> 21:08.910
she took her cousin away from her.

21:09.240 --> 21:13.840
It didn't seem like the cousin would end up 
unhappy just by being with Iwanaga-san.

21:13.840 --> 21:15.040
I'm not sure.

21:15.040 --> 21:19.420
They might get along right now, but who 
knows what might happen in the future?

21:19.830 --> 21:23.420
So was your explanation about 
that apartment actually true?

21:23.420 --> 21:24.630
Who knows?

21:24.630 --> 21:26.320
It's not like I could guess the truth

21:26.320 --> 21:28.940
with so little information 
and no preparation.

21:29.710 --> 21:33.180
The third man who committed suicide 
was incredibly insensitive

21:33.180 --> 21:36.210
and couldn't actually 
care less that his ex died.

21:36.210 --> 21:39.940
For all we know, he might've been 
ecstatic at how cheap the rent was.

21:39.940 --> 21:43.670
He might've been tricked and 
his only way out was suicide,

21:43.670 --> 21:48.320
and his relatives might be keeping it 
a secret because of how shameful he is.

21:48.320 --> 21:51.440
What I presented was an answer 
that didn't contradict reality,

21:51.440 --> 21:55.580
was the easiest to swallow, and wouldn't 
leave a bad taste in their mouths.

21:55.960 --> 21:59.790
The only thing necessary 
back there was an explanation

21:59.790 --> 22:02.590
that would ease the manager's worries.

22:02.590 --> 22:04.460
I figured as much, but...

22:04.460 --> 22:07.220
And I wasn't being irresponsible.

22:07.220 --> 22:10.440
It's true that nothing is 
haunting that apartment,

22:10.440 --> 22:13.220
so there won't be any supernatural 
incidents there in the future.

22:13.600 --> 22:15.640
Besides, there's no way any ghosts would dwell

22:15.640 --> 22:17.600
in an apartment Rikka-san lived in.

22:17.600 --> 22:19.930
She has the same body as you,

22:19.930 --> 22:23.550
so all the supernatural beings would 
consider her horrifying or smelly.

22:24.110 --> 22:26.740
Even if something was 
haunting it, they'd run away.

22:26.740 --> 22:31.290
And in that case, they would've 
told me about her even sooner.

22:40.140 --> 22:42.460
We have to stop Rikka-san 
as soon as possible.

22:42.920 --> 22:47.340
But I wonder how Rikka-san 
was describing me to those people.

22:47.340 --> 22:50.140
I'm certain she made it sound 
like I'm an awful woman.

22:50.140 --> 22:54.430
Well, considering you're not scared 
of anything, you can be pretty awful.

22:54.430 --> 22:57.060
Of course, even I have 
something I'm scared of.

22:57.060 --> 22:58.310
Like what?

22:58.310 --> 23:01.670
No fire bells. It'll ruin everything.

23:02.310 --> 23:04.990
Now you're quoting the 
rakugo story "The Fire Drum."

23:04.990 --> 23:08.360
Impressive, Kuro-senpai. 
You're nothing like Rikka-san.

23:08.360 --> 23:11.750
Would you stop trying to hide 
behind rakugo punchlines?

23:11.750 --> 23:15.210
That doesn't actually 
make you smart or anything.

23:15.210 --> 23:17.960
Well, I can't think of anything else.

23:21.130 --> 23:24.130
Relationships between a man 
and a woman tend to go better

23:24.130 --> 23:26.190
if they have a secret or two.

23:47.020 --> 23:50.030
To be continued
